      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T17:07:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Finally got around to putting together a test: https://skottie.skia.org/a528a84a5e1455021ad7f7c75f73a70c?h\u003d500\u0026w\u003d500\n\nA few issues:\n\n1) sksl inputs and outputs are premultiplied, but the hard mix logic is expressed in unpremultiplied space -- so we need to unpremul/premul explicitly.\n\n2) floor() is almost sufficient, except for the edge case of both components \u003d\u003d 1, in which case it would yield 2.  We still need to clamp explicitly to 1 (min).\n\n3) The Adobe description is incomplete: after computing the component values, the result is composited onto dest using srcOver.\n\nHere\u0027s what I have working, you may want to expand for clarity:\n\n    // HardMix blending.\n    // (https://helpx.adobe.com/photoshop/using/blending-modes.html).\n    src.rgb \u003d min(floor(unpremul(src).rgb + unpremul(dst).rgb), 1)*src.a;\n    \n    // Composite back to dst using srcOver.\n    return src + (1 - src.a)*dst;",
      "parentUuid": "fe5f6a17_f58843a5",
      "revId": "b8e195c7c86a97d2ee674eb6d27aac1c2760bd79",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
